From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 01:42:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 426/488] [DS4.1] The drafter's Markov embeddings in its own
 kernels

Each vocabulary-parallel greedy draft step embedded the previous token
with nn.Embedding (an index_select), the first step after a torch gather
of the anchor tokens, and the confidence head read the embeddings through
a stack: seven torch kernels a decode step in the draft graph. With a
replicated BF16 W1 (production), one kernel now looks up the anchors'
rows, and each step's argmax selection also writes the selected token's
row for the next step, both into the step's buffer and into the
(request, step) buffer the confidence head reads. Rows are copied
exactly; tested against nn.Embedding.
